# security.mdc
## Security Baseline

### REQUIRED
- Define security headers appropriate for hosting environment.
- CSP required:
  - Report-only in development is acceptable
  - Enforced in production
- Permissions-Policy must be defined (deny by default, allow only what is needed).
- No client-side secrets (keys/tokens must stay server-side).
- Validate and sanitize all untrusted inputs.
- Rate limit public endpoints where feasible.

### REQUIRED (Auth & Sessions)
- Use secure cookies for sessions where applicable.
- Enforce session timeouts.
- Least privilege access for server actions.

### FORBIDDEN
- Disabling security features to “make it work”
- Shipping debug endpoints or verbose error leaks in production
